{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>YHWH shall reign, etc.</b> The reason they did not say ״YHWH reigned״ — they themselves gave the reason: ״for [he] came,״ etc., meaning, because the judgment was carried out upon only one nation, and that is His saying <b>for Pharaoh's horse came</b>, etc. — for from this there is no negation of all the deities whom the nations worship, and therefore His kingship is not recognized in the world. Not so in the future to come, when HaShem will execute judgment upon all the nations — then YHWH will be King over all the earth, and that is the meaning of ״YHWH shall reign.״" "<b>Or</b> it may intend the reason for His saying <b>shall reign</b> and not ״reigned״ — [namely] ״Pharaoh's horse came,״ etc., meaning, they were all in the drowning like a single horse. And the intention in this is that not a single one of them escaped, just as if one person drowns, all of them drown. And this is true: had the matter been proclaimed to the world — the magnitude and awesomeness of the miracle — so that the world would recognize the greatness of the might, the splendor of victory, and the foundation of our faith, all who heard would be inflamed and say: ascribe honor, for this is our Master, our King, and from now YHWH shall be King — except that they did not walk on dry land and none escaped besides the children of Israel, as it says ״and the children of Israel walked,״ etc. And to [the nations] the nations will not hearken, for they are touched by the matter insofar as He is their god."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:31.355047811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}